Perhaps not the first rule in scripts; but not nonsense. No user 
application script should make asssumptions about the file structure 
outside of the application directory; or, the location from which the 
application is installed. Those structures outside the application which 
will be called inside the application should be abstracted with variables.
In creating the environment in which the script executes, one command 
should store the results of the "pwd" command (or equivalent "cd" in 
DOS). Then all following references to file locations should reference 
(chomp $you_are_here)='pwd')/foo



